## Artifact Collection

Save artifacts incrementally so partial work survives timeouts:

```bash
mkdir -p /logs/agent/artifacts
cp experiment_review.md /logs/agent/artifacts/ 2>/dev/null
cp review.json /logs/agent/artifacts/ 2>/dev/null
cp preflight_repair.md /logs/agent/artifacts/ 2>/dev/null
cp revised_experiment_protocol.md /logs/agent/artifacts/ 2>/dev/null
cp -r predicted_results/ /logs/agent/artifacts/predicted_results/ 2>/dev/null
cp -r figures/ /logs/agent/artifacts/figures/ 2>/dev/null
cp latex/template.pdf /logs/agent/artifacts/paper.pdf 2>/dev/null
cp latex/template.tex /logs/agent/artifacts/paper.tex 2>/dev/null
cp latex/references.bib /logs/agent/artifacts/references.bib 2>/dev/null
cp -r literature/ /logs/agent/artifacts/literature/ 2>/dev/null
cp -r submissions/ /logs/agent/artifacts/submissions/ 2>/dev/null
```

Only `/logs/agent/` and `/logs/verifier/` are mounted to the host. Do not write to
other `/logs/` subpaths.
